{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A night of watching, etc.</b> The verse intends to allude to five wondrous miracles whose time is this night: 1, in the days of Abraham, when he struck the four kings (Genesis 14:15) ״וַיֵּחָלֵק עֲלֵיהֶם לַיְלָה״. 2, at the exodus from Egypt, as it is written (Exodus 12:29) ״וַיְהִי בַּחֲצִי הַלַּיְלָה״. 3, in the days of Hezekiah, when Gabriel struck the camp of Sennacherib, as it is written (II Kings 19:35) ״וַיְהִי בַּלַּיְלָה הַהוּא״. 4, in the days of Mordecai and Esther (Esther 6:1) ״בַּלַּיְלָה הַהוּא נָדְדָה שְׁנַת הַמֶּלֶךְ״. 5, the future redemption." "Corresponding to the miracle of Abraham it says <b>a night of watching it is to HaShem</b>, for through the medium of the miracle the truth of Him, may He be blessed, was revealed, as they said, their memory for blessing (Genesis Rabbah 42:1), that there were some among the nations who did not believe in the miracle of His saving him from Ur Kasdim but did believe in the miracle of the striking of the four kings. And corresponding to Egypt it says <b>to bring them out of the land of Egypt.</b> And corresponding to the miracle of Hezekiah it says <b>it is the night</b> known to you, as written in the words of the prophet (II Kings 19:35) ״וַיְהִי בַּלַּיְלָה הַהוּא וַיֵּצֵא מַלְאַךְ״ etc. And corresponding to the miracle of Mordecai it says <b>this one to HaShem</b>, and corresponding to the future redemption it says <b>watching for all the children of Israel throughout their generations</b> — its meaning is, at the end of the generations, swiftly and in our time."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:24.183943609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}